# Copy to .env. Nothing here is required: with no backend reachable the engine
# runs its deterministic path, and the run receipt reports zero model calls
# rather than the two the design intends.

# --- Model backend --------------------------------------------------------
# ollama (default, local, no account) | openai (any compatible endpoint) | none
WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND=ollama

# Apache 2.0, unrestricted commercial use, no user ceiling. qwen2.5:7b-instruct
# is the same licence and a drop-in alternative. Llama is not the default: its
# community licence caps commercial use at 700M MAU and fails the Open Source
# Definition, which makes it a poor template for client delivery.
WHYCHAIN_LLM_MODEL=mistral:7b-instruct

# Only for the hosted path. Groq, Together, OpenRouter, vLLM and LM Studio all
# serve the same open weights behind this API.
#   WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND=openai
#   WHYCHAIN_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   WHYCHAIN_LLM_API_KEY=
#   WHYCHAIN_LLM_MODEL=mistral-7b-instruct

# A remote Ollama, or a second local model, without disturbing the hosted
# settings above. These belong to the local backend alone; WHYCHAIN_LLM_MODEL
# and WHYCHAIN_LLM_BASE_URL belong to whichever backend WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND
# names, and to both when it names neither.
# WHYCHAIN_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://gpu-box:11434
# WHYCHAIN_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b-instruct

# Per-stage overrides, if the two jobs want different models. Extraction is
# classification and runs well on a small model; the narrative is the harder of
# the two.
# WHYCHAIN_INTENT_MODEL=
# WHYCHAIN_EXPANSION_MODEL=
# WHYCHAIN_EXTRACTION_MODEL=
# WHYCHAIN_NARRATIVE_MODEL=

# ── A hosted endpoint, for when a laptop cannot spare the memory ────────────
# `OpenAICompatibleModel` speaks the API that Groq, Together, OpenRouter, vLLM,
# LM Studio and Google all implement, so switching provider is configuration
# rather than code. Nothing in the engine changes; that is what the protocol is
# for. Set WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND=openai to force this path.
#
# Google Gemini, via its OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Materially faster than a
# 7B on a laptop, which matters because objective 8 names latency as a
# constraint. Note the trade the engine states rather than hides: inference
# leaves the boundary, which is the sovereignty argument the local default is
# there to make. Both are offered; the choice is visible in the console.
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND=openai
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_API_KEY=       # never commit this; .env is gitignored

# How long any single model call may take before the deterministic path stands
# in for it. A demo that waits is a demo that fails.
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_TIMEOUT=45

# Set to `off` to measure what the model really costs rather than what a warm
# cache costs. The benchmark forces the deterministic path regardless.
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_CACHE=off

# ── OpenRouter, free tier ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The best fit of the hosted options, because the free models it serves are the
# *same open weights* the local default runs -- Mistral, Qwen, Gemma under their
# own licences -- so the governance argument survives the move and only the
# latency changes. `_hosted_identity()` reads the licence off the model id, and
# names Llama as not open source rather than lumping it in.
#
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_FREE_ONLY refuses any model id without the provider's free
# marker. A key with credit on it will bill happily for a mistyped paid model
# and the mistake is invisible until an invoice arrives, so this is a refusal
# rather than a warning: the backend reports itself unavailable, the engine
# takes the deterministic path, and the console says why.
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_BACKEND=openai
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_MODEL=mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct:free
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_FREE_ONLY=1
# WHYCHAIN_LLM_API_KEY=       # never commit this; .env is gitignored
